1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,521
Good morning, North College Library.

2
00:00:02,521 --> 00:00:03,590
How can I help you?

3
00:00:03,590 --> 00:00:06,740
I was wondering if it was possible to join the library.

4
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:09,000
Are you a student at North College?

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:09,791
No, I'm not,

6
00:00:09,791 --> 00:00:13,220
but someone told me it was possible to join, even if I wasn't.

7
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:14,737
That's right, it is.

8
00:00:14,737 --> 00:00:16,254
Are you over 18?

9
00:00:16,254 --> 00:00:18,150
That's our minimum joining age.

10
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:19,371
Yes, I am.

11
00:00:19,371 --> 00:00:21,000
That's no problem then.

12
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,900
Could you tell me what I have to do to join?

13
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:28,667
Well, you'll need to come in to the library and fill out some forms.

14
00:00:28,667 --> 00:00:32,073
You'll also need to bring two passport photos with you.

15
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:34,456
We also need two documents for ID,

16
00:00:34,456 --> 00:00:36,840
so a driving licence would be fine.

17
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:39,560
I've got that and what else?

18
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:40,920
A credit card?

19
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:43,900
No, it needs to have your address on it.

20
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:46,840
Shall I bring a bank statement, would that do?

21
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:47,820
That'll be fine.

22
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:48,301
Good.

23
00:00:48,301 --> 00:00:51,190
Does it cost anything to join?

24
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:56,275
Well, it's free for students here but otherwise it's ￡125 per year

25
00:00:56,275 --> 00:01:01,360
or ￡25 if you've got a current student card from another college.

26
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:07,301
I was at Westerley College until last year but now I've got a job

27
00:01:07,301 --> 00:01:08,998
at Jefferson's steel factory.

28
00:01:08,998 --> 00:01:11,968
Er, it's more expensive than I thought.

29
00:01:11,968 --> 00:01:14,090
My local library is free.

30
00:01:14,090 --> 00:01:17,258
But you'll find they don't have the range of reference books

31
00:01:17,258 --> 00:01:19,562
or facilities which we buy for our students.

32
00:01:19,562 --> 00:01:22,730
That's why you have to pay to be an external member.

33
00:01:22,730 --> 00:01:23,732
I see.

34
00:01:23,732 --> 00:01:26,740
How many books can I borrow?

35
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:31,546
We allow twelve items borrowed at any one time if you're a student,

36
00:01:31,546 --> 00:01:34,133
and that includes CDs, DVDs and videos.

37
00:01:34,133 --> 00:01:37,830
However, it's only eight items for members of the public.

38
00:01:37,830 --> 00:01:38,200
Fine.

39
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:41,160
And how long can I have them for?

40
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:46,970
Well, you can have both fiction and reference books for four weeks which isn't

41
00:01:46,970 --> 00:01:47,800
bad really.

42
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:50,100
And what happens if I return them late?

43
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:53,410
Like all libraries there's a fine system in place.

44
00:01:53,410 --> 00:01:58,826
The minimum fine is 1.50 but it can be much higher for some items-up

45
00:01:58,826 --> 00:02:00,270
to 5 per week.

46
00:02:00,270 --> 00:02:03,540
We'll give you a booklet with all the details when you join.

47
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:09,812
You can always renew items if they're not required by anyone else by telephoning

48
00:02:09,812 --> 00:02:12,500
or logging on to our website.

49
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:13,835
What about the computers?

50
00:02:13,835 --> 00:02:16,170
Can I use them free of charge?

51
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:17,970
For college students it's free,

52
00:02:17,970 --> 00:02:21,930
but for external members like yourself, the first hour is free

53
00:02:21,930 --> 00:02:26,250
and then we make a nominal charge of ￡1 per hour thereafter.

54
00:02:26,250 --> 00:02:28,850
Do I have to book in advance for them?

55
00:02:28,850 --> 00:02:30,208
Oh, yes, it's advisable.

56
00:02:30,208 --> 00:02:34,962
Most people tend to book twenty-four hours in advance although sometimes you can get

57
00:02:34,962 --> 00:02:37,000
one with only six hours' notice.

58
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,519
However, the earliest you can book a computer is forty-eight hours before you need

59
00:02:41,519 --> 00:02:41,842
it,

60
00:02:41,842 --> 00:02:45,070
and you can only book one hour at a time.

61
00:02:45,070 --> 00:02:49,332
If no-one else has booked the computer out, then you may be able to

62
00:02:49,332 --> 00:02:51,158
have another hour if you want.

63
00:02:51,158 --> 00:02:53,289
We have a wide range of databases,

64
00:02:53,289 --> 00:02:55,420
so the computers are in great demand.

65
00:02:55,420 --> 00:03:01,740
I'm thinking of doing some writing and I might need to access national newspapers.

66
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:04,900
Do you have them on these databases?

67
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:05,984
We do indeed.

68
00:03:05,984 --> 00:03:10,683
We've got all the big nationals, The Guardian and The Observer, The Independent

69
00:03:10,683 --> 00:03:12,851
and The Times and Sunday Times.

70
00:03:12,851 --> 00:03:17,550
We've also got all the local papers and a wide selection of magazines.

71
00:03:17,550 --> 00:03:18,154
Excellent.

72
00:03:18,154 --> 00:03:21,780
I assume you have photocopying facilities?

73
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:22,537
Of course.

74
00:03:22,537 --> 00:03:26,320
5p a sheet for both A4 and A3 black-and-white copies

75
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:28,590
and 40p a sheet for colour.

76
00:03:28,590 --> 00:03:33,130
You can get a card from the counter here-it doesn't take coins.

77
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:33,555
OK.

78
00:03:33,555 --> 00:03:39,501
Oh by the way, another thing I was wondering about was if you ran

79
00:03:39,501 --> 00:03:42,050
any writing classes through the library?

80
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:42,823
We do,

81
00:03:42,823 --> 00:03:46,686
but you'll have to speak to John Grantingham about that.

82
00:03:46,686 --> 00:03:48,232
He's our resident author.

83
00:03:48,232 --> 00:03:50,550
He runs the creative writing classes.

84
00:03:50,550 --> 00:03:51,021
John...

85
00:03:51,021 --> 00:03:51,492
Grant...

86
00:03:51,492 --> 00:03:54,790
Could you spell that for me please?

87
00:03:54,790 --> 00:03:55,550
Certainly.

88
00:03:55,550 --> 00:04:03,910
G - R - A - N - T - I - N - G - H - A - M.

89
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:06,770
Are the classes here at the library?

90
00:04:06,770 --> 00:04:12,608
Yes-he's here on Thursday evenings, oh no sorry, Friday-he's just changed it.

91
00:04:12,608 --> 00:04:16,500
You can contact him by emailing the library.

92
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:16,964
Okay.

93
00:04:16,964 --> 00:04:21,141
Right, well that's about all I need to know.

94
00:04:21,141 --> 00:04:22,069
Thank you.

95
00:04:22,069 --> 00:04:25,782
I'll be along later this week to join.

96
00:04:25,782 --> 00:04:26,246
Thanks.

97
00:04:26,246 --> 00:04:26,710
Bye.
